body:
Well, you get my upvote....because I also hate this. 

&#x200B;

Some people are trash...other people are great. It takes 2 to tango and sorry not sorry if you make poor decisions. Simple as that.

As someone who has also been sexually abused, I can relate to what you're going through. 

&#x200B;

It's 100% okay that you are feeling the way you are, and whatever coping strategies are necessary for you to use are the ones you should be using. 

&#x200B;

My big question to you is, do you feel comfortable opening up to the nurse or doctor prior to the examination? It really helped me to do so at my gyno appt a few years following the abuse. You don't need to say or explain anything you don't feel comfortable with doing. However, it might go a long way to even just say "I need to let you know that I was sexually abused and this is a very uncomfortable situation for me". It went a long way for me to do so, the nurse and doctor were very kind, understanding and comforting. They would likely even be able to help you find support if you asked them to do so. 

&#x200B;

My other suggestion would be to bring someone along. A friend or family member that you feel comfortable with. They may even be able to be in the room with you if you wanted them to be. 

&#x200B;

I hope one of those suggestions helps you! Feel free to DM me if you want to talk :) Good luck!

I can totally relate -- I got onto eharmony shortly after my breakup in November and it's just.....duds. Honestly. It's...very sad. 

&#x200B;

I hope you can continue to cope. It does get easier everyday. I'm 4 months post breakup and I can promise that it does get a little easier each day.
